# Line-ending policy
#
# Everything git detects as text is stored in the repository with LF and checked
# out with the platform's native endings. This relies on git's content-based
# detection rather than an extension whitelist, which keeps it correct for file
# types nobody has thought to list yet - and for *.obj, which in this repository
# is a Wavefront mesh (text) rather than a compiler object file (binary).
#
# Without this, a file once committed with CRLF stays that way, and the next
# contributor whose core.autocrlf normalizes it produces a diff touching every
# line of the file (ChPac02Tire.cpp was one such case).
* text=auto

# Files whose endings must be fixed regardless of the checkout platform.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

data/** -linguist-detectable
